        <item>
            <title>3.3.0</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 29 Jun 2026 12:32:56 +0100</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Deveshb15/aura</link>
            <sparkle:version>30</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>3.3.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Carpet 3.3.0 — stability &amp; memory</h2>
<p>A reliability-focused release that tackles the high-RAM and occasional-crash reports.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Lower memory use.</strong> Screenshots and previews are now decoded at a downsampled size (OCR, thumbnails, link images), and image work happens off the main thread — so big captures no longer spike RAM or stall the UI.</li>
  <li><strong>Survives a damaged library.</strong> If the data file is corrupted (e.g. after a hard shutdown), Carpet now recovers and keeps running instead of failing to launch. Your saved files on disk are safe.</li>
  <li><strong>Leaner under load.</strong> The library grid renders on demand as you scroll, the search index has a memory ceiling, and network fetches are size-capped.</li>
  <li><strong>Grid fixes.</strong> Switching filters now re-balances the layout correctly, and cards no longer overlap.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/Deveshb15/aura/releases/download/v3.3.0/Carpet-3.3.0.dmg" length="18221716" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="zIHxUoxjSpi4+M61zGsjVkUQa1SkxnBRA3qKA/anFQoequeNhbFVPeTh8X/78PCXdM0+4TL3Z85f4MmD8Tp6BA=="/>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title>3.2.1</title>
